Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): a project added to T3 asks once whether to start a
 jstack home for it

Once every project and thread has loaded, a project added with no jbus home shows "Start a
jstack home for <project>?" with Yes and Not now. Yes starts a home as its root row's "Start a
home" does; Not now, or closing the toast, leaves that action on the row.

The client keeps the projects it has seen in localStorage, so a project is asked about once,
ever. The first load counts every project there as seen and asks about none, and a project
added with a home is seen without an ask.
